            thing has changed.

     rreevveerrtt--bbuuffffeerr
            Revert the current buffer to the latest file on disk.

     ssaavvee--bbuuffffeerr
            Save the contents of the current buffer if it has been changed,
            optionally creating a backup copy.

     ssaavvee--bbuuffffeerrss--kkiillll--eemmaaccss
